<DocLayout title="A real update, end to end" eyebrow="Reproducible walkthrough" description="Execute the native service, acknowledge a real deletion and insertion, query committed versions, and reopen the durable store." next={{label:"Production contracts", href:"/production/"}}>
  <p>No browser simulation. This trace is produced by the installed Python package and verified by the site’s example checks. The graph is an eight-vertex degree-four ring; it is not a throughput benchmark.</p>
  <div class="trace"><Replay /></div>
  <h2>Run the same path</h2>
  <p>Install from source with a C++17 compiler on a supported local POSIX environment. The temporary directory below deliberately isolates this disposable example; use a persistent private directory in your application.</p>
  <pre data-verify="python" data-copy={example}><code>{example}</code></pre>
  <h2>What is actually checked?</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Delete edge zero-one and wait for durable acknowledgment. Committed version becomes two and vertex zero has no partner.</li>
    <li>Reinsert the same edge. Version three restores partner one; the matching check passes after each change.</li>
    <li>Close and reopen the SQLite store. The query recovers version three and partner one. Retrying request two returns the original outcome without another mutation; changing its payload rejects. All eight partners and every possible edge are checked after recovery and rejection.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>SQLite commit precedes successful receipt completion. A receipt timeout does not cancel accepted work. Multi-query snapshots and arbitrary network storage are not implied by this example.</p>
</DocLayout>
